{"duration_api_ms":37023,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"cc061a12-c583-4e68-95de-dcb1a3e4b80a","total_cost_usd":0.039379199999999996,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":40626,"output_tokens":3125,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2389},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3125,"cache_read_input_tokens":40626,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":3125,"cacheReadInputTokens":40626,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.039379199999999996,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":2389,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Bottom line: use the 3PL now.** The numbers don't support building yet, and a split only makes sense after you already have a warehouse to fill.\n\n**The math**\n\n- West coast volume: 35% × 4,500/week ≈ 1,575 orders/week ≈ 82,000/year\n- 3PL cost at current volume: 82,000 × $3.10 ≈ **$254,000/year**, scales linearly, no capital risk\n- Warehouse fixed cost: $420,000 lease + 8 hires (assuming ~$50K fully loaded each ≈ $400K) ≈ **$820,000/year**, before racking, WMS software, utilities, insurance, or packaging supplies — so treat that as a floor, not a ceiling\n\n**Breakeven volume**: $820,000 ÷ $3.10 ≈ 264,500 orders/year ≈ 5,100 orders/week on the west coast — roughly **3.2x your current west-coast volume** (or ~14,600 total weekly orders company-wide if the 35% mix holds). Below that, the 3PL is cheaper on cost alone; the warehouse only starts paying for itself past that line, and it's a 3-year lease so you're locked in either way.\n\n**The tradeoff that isn't in the math**: the 3PL gives up control over packaging (brand/unboxing experience) and returns handling. If either is a real differentiator or cost driver for you today, that's worth paying a premium for — but the premium here is roughly $570K/year at current volume, which is a lot to pay for control before you've proven the volume is there.\n\n**Recommendation**: go 3PL now, and set a trigger to revisit — once west-coast volume approaches ~5,000+ orders/week (or you have visibility into growth that gets you there within the 3-year window), build the warehouse. A \"split\" doesn't make sense as a starting position; it's a good pattern *after* you have a warehouse, sending overflow/peak volume to a 3PL rather than hiring for peak capacity.\n\nOne gap: I assumed ~$50K fully loaded per hire since it wasn't given — if actual wages are meaningfully different, or you have a specific west-coast growth rate, I can redo the breakeven with real numbers.","ttft_ms":28972,"type":"result","duration_ms":37151,"uuid":"64a73b1d-9e40-440f-ace8-42757ea68dd9","ttft_stream_ms":1631,"time_to_request_ms":74,"first_content_frame_ms":1631,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
